    "body": "Fixes #41923.\n\n## What\n\n`generate_prefill_cuda_graph_batch_sizes` filtered the grid with `s <= max_bs` but never appended `max_bs` itself, so an off-grid `--cuda-graph-max-bs-prefill` silently rounded down to the nearest captured bucket (3000 → 2816, 4500 → 4096, 4607 → 4096). The decode path appends the ceiling when it is off-grid, and the CPU graph path unions it in; prefill was the odd one out. Since `post_capture_kv_sizing_planned()` treats the largest captured bucket as the prefill ceiling, an off-grid value also quietly disabled post-capture KV sizing (the #33847 failure mode).\n\nThe change mirrors decode: append `max_bs` when it is not on the grid.\n\n## Verification\n\nNew `test/registered/cpu/test_cuda_graph_batch_sizes.py` (CPU lane, no GPU needed):\n\n- off-grid ceilings (3000, 4500, 4607, 5000, 6000, 10000) now end exactly at the ceiling and stay sorted\n- on-grid ceiling (2048) is not duplicated\n- ceiling below the first grid point (`2`) yields `[2]` instead of an empty list\n- decode parity pinned with a real `ServerArgs`\n\nAll 5 pass locally on this branch; with the fix reverted the 3 off-grid tests fail, so they pin the changed behavior.\n\nNot run locally: GPU capture e2e (no GPU on this machine). The change only alters which batch sizes get captured; capture itself is exercised by the existing CUDA graph CI lanes.\n\n## Risk / rollback\n\nOne conditional append in bucket-list generation. Rollback is a revert; the pre-fix behavior is a strict subset of the post-fix bucket list, so reverting never removes a bucket anyone could have relied on.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36785544212](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36785544212)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36785543817](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36785543817)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36785544279](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36785544279)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
